sentences.text:
7. Considering the submissions made at the bar and on perusal of the various statements as well as the postmortem report, there are no sign against the applicant to suggest that soon before her death,
the victim was subjected to any physical or mental harassment in relation to any demand of dowry;
the ingredients which are prima facie necessary for implicating the applicant under Sections 304B of IPC are absent coupled with the fact that the applicant has no criminal antecedents and is languishing in jail since 24.04.2024, I am of the view that the applicant is entitled to be released on bail.

